NOT RUN (the person who wrote the sheet)
  - PRE-REGISTERED in out/vwap_hunt_2026-10-20/PREREG.md before any run; nothing tuned on a result.
  - 1-MINUTE SHEETS run the New York passes only (machine time); 5 / 15-minute sheets every pass the family runs except pre (08:25-09:30), which the brief does not ask for.
  - THE SESSION VWAP of the engine restarts at every pass start (09:30, 11:00, 13:30; 03:00 London; 00:00 Asia; 18:00 evening); 'rth' / 'us' anchors stay at 09:30 for the New York passes.
  - THE CAP: 4 trades per session pass (several passes: a day can hold more, and a trade of one pass may still be open when the next pass enters).
  - COSTS AND FILLS: the engine's own (1 tick of slippage, $4 a round turn, tick replay).
  - THE TEST DAYS are read only by `bp.py taught wf` (the 3:1 block walk-forward, once), its output sent to a log unread until SELECTION.md is written.

ALSO TRUE OF THE RUN (the lane)
  - CAPPED PER SESSION PASS, NOT PER DAY: max_trades 4 counts inside each pass (3 passes: nyam, mid, pm), so a day can hold up to 12 trades; a family's own loss or trade count (max_loss) counts inside one pass too.
  - The passes are independent: a trade of one pass may still be open when another pass enters (one position at a time holds inside a pass only).
  - Every trade is flat by 15:58 ET (13:13 on an equity half day); no entry in the last 5 minutes of a pass.
  - Costs: $4.00 a round turn and 1 tick of slippage on market and stop fills, 1 contract (the engine's own).

HONEST LIMITS
  - One video's rule, read on the build days (2021-09-22 .. 2025-06-30): in-sample.
  - The family's settings and the exits are the video's own: nothing was tuned, searched or picked.
  - The neighbours are shown to see how fragile the rule is; they are not alternatives to choose from.
  - The unseen days (2025-07-01 on) were not read: a person has to ask for that, and it is read once.
  - The random entries are the pipeline's own (any bar of the session pass, matched by day and pass): they do not wait for the family's entry window.
